  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material and visual material of the meme",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the meme's textual material (the caption 'for those that dont like smiling probably due to their constant painful hip they all seem to grasp') and visual material (Kevin_Hart's image), as the meme implicitly addresses the user by framing the stereotype as a commentary on 'people' in general, and by using Kevin Hart's public persona to represent the targeted group. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the meme's structure and intent project the user as the one who might hold or be exposed to this harmful stereotype, making them a recipient of the message.",
